{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787706224376261002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"kilted-nuclear-bronco","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"5cea481572d389182ad2aad1c78fdaea01ca657e3cf9d6efb99372aa745f4834","event_uuid":"09fd3bcc-5d12-4437-b6a4-b3b8cd839cbe","position":{"commit_sha":"1d5ebd41d3658b2958eab260ba14e13272ca3a62","position":"1787706108664123001-09fd3bcc-5d12-4437-b6a4-b3b8cd839cbe"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e3fff0cf2e4d55121cec9a825d2237e0fe293fbc8c92979676a0957933aaf135","event_uuid":"291bbe90-3e09-4120-8461-38d138063fc2","position":{"commit_sha":"d7e86e2ba423d3bbb73d2d3c87c643d4f7ebee31","position":"1787706162192161001-291bbe90-3e09-4120-8461-38d138063fc2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"e41b6294696593ac0f8a051f74f1067e7b35e9e1b9d69e4d3cbf53daf974f5c7","event_uuid":"ba50f7b8-54a0-495c-9c2c-842d34eec5e0","position":{"commit_sha":"fcf39d96ed0edb183a119d3d905f00cfdb3a7d0f","position":"1787706198311058001-ba50f7b8-54a0-495c-9c2c-842d34eec5e0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3d0c8a5fbc7b1596aa83afff6d81b8e14b4fa0306bab53a0287dec37d30c7e89","event_uuid":"f16bd8ec-2881-40a9-95d0-863fdf99339a","position":{"commit_sha":"9d25e3e8c16776ba9e23aa31eea0b41c75f528b6","position":"1787706224376261001-f16bd8ec-2881-40a9-95d0-863fdf99339a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787706108664123001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"291bbe90-3e09-4120-8461-38d138063fc2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"44fd-230c-5893-4246"},{"link_uuid":"ba50f7b8-54a0-495c-9c2c-842d34eec5e0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d9ab-7b5e-fe4c-4ff4"},{"link_uuid":"f16bd8ec-2881-40a9-95d0-863fdf99339a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6af7-edb7-88ce-4110"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nThe `mcp` compose service has **no mechanism anywhere in the repo** to populate the ticket\nstore its tools read. The step is ABSENT, not failing. The deployed server at\n`https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` therefore serves a store that does not exist.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp:42` — `COPY . /app` is the only thing placing files at `/app`;\n  `:60` is a bare `CMD [\"rebar-mcp\"]`. No clone, no init, no entrypoint.\n- `.dockerignore:7` excludes `.tickets-tracker` (`:5` excludes `.git`), and the build context is\n  the repo root — so `/app/.tickets-tracker` **cannot** be baked into the image by construction.\n- `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:372-373` — the `mcp` service declares only two secret\n  volumes. No tracker mount.\n- `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` is set for exactly one service, the review-bot\n  (`docker-compose.yml:129`). `REBAR_ROOT` appears nowhere in `infra/`.\n- Blue-green reproduces the same shape: `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh:346-368` mounts only\n  secrets and sets no tracker env.\n- `infra/scripts/compose-up.sh:30` provisions a `reviewbot-tickets` site dir; nothing for mcp.\n  `infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh:91-94` provisions a tickets PAT only for the review-bot.\n- `docs/adr/0104-mcp-on-box.md` has zero occurrences of tracker/tickets/store/clone.\n- `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` has a single commit, `8297083532a3` (\"Add rebar-mcp HTTP\n  service to the AWS box\"); the test added in that same commit,\n  `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py`, asserts nothing about a store.\n\nWhy the path is `/app/.tickets-tracker`: `rebar.toml` has no `[tracker]` section so the default\n`.tickets-tracker` applies (`src/rebar/config.py:138-155`); with `.git` dockerignored, `/app` is\nnot a work tree, `git rev-parse` fails and is swallowed at `src/rebar/_config_sources.py:102-103`,\nfalling back to `Path.cwd()` = `/app` (`WORKDIR`, `Dockerfile.mcp:33`).\n\nThe review-bot has the mechanism that was never applied to mcp:\n`infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:153-155` (entrypoint clone) converged by\n`infra/scripts/reviewbot-ensure-tickets.sh`.\n\n## Observed impact\n\n    list_tickets / search / ready_tickets  -> []                    (silent)\n    show_ticket <real alias>               -> \"ticket_not_found\"\n    fsck                                   -> \"ticket system not initialized (/app/.tickets-tracker not found)\"\n\nHost: EC2 `i-00880b2c7f13527c5` (`rebar-gerrit`, us-east-1, 52.3.128.230), up since 2026-07-13.\nAny agent session that trusted an empty `list_tickets` from this endpoint may have filed\nduplicate tickets.\n\n## Open design questions (need an operator decision before implementing)\n\n1. Should this server serve the shared `tickets` branch at all, or only certified LLM ops\n   (`review_plan`/`verify_completion`)? Those materialize a pinned store via\n   `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:672`, which still needs a live tracker or an origin on\n   disk — so they likely fail too. Worth confirming whether they have EVER succeeded on the box.\n2. Dedicated volume (e.g. `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`) or share the existing\n   `reviewbot-tickets` store? Sharing puts two writers on one store; the write lock handles it,\n   but it was not designed for that.\n3. Read-only or writer? `REBAR_MCP_READONLY` is currently unset. A writer needs a tickets PAT\n   that `fetch-secrets.sh` does not provision for mcp.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The `mcp` service starts with a usable ticket store, or is explicitly configured and\n      documented as not serving tracker reads.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` (or a sibling) asserts the store provisioning, so\n      this gap cannot ship silently again.\n- [ ] `docs/adr/0104-mcp-on-box.md` records the decision taken for the three questions above.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","44fd-230c-5893-4246"],["relates_to","6af7-edb7-88ce-4110"],["relates_to","d9ab-7b5e-fe4c-4ff4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["infra","mcp","deploy","data-integrity"],"ticket_id":"0bd6-c3b2-d9a8-45b2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"mcp compose service never provisions a ticket store, so every MCP tracker read on the deployed server is empty","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["09fd3bcc-5d12-4437-b6a4-b3b8cd839cbe","291bbe90-3e09-4120-8461-38d138063fc2","ba50f7b8-54a0-495c-9c2c-842d34eec5e0","f16bd8ec-2881-40a9-95d0-863fdf99339a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787706224376261002,"uuid":"c66aeaa4-7326-4128-b353-7cf0f7e89331"}